{
  "name": "Test a refund approval limit with synthetic webhook requests",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nThis workflow decides whether a fictional refund request can proceed automatically. Send the amount in USD cents to the webhook. Positive whole amounts up to and including 5000 cents produce a simulated refund event. Larger or invalid amounts produce a handoff event for a fictional reviewer. Both responses are JSON, so you can inspect the decision in n8n or check it from your terminal. The demo never contacts a payment provider or creates a review ticket.\n\n### Setup\nImport this file into a local n8n instance and publish the workflow. POST a JSON object containing `amount_cents` to the production webhook at `/webhook/aw-demo-refund-approval`. Start with 8000 for a handoff, then try 5000 for a simulated approval. The accompanying AugmentWorks packet checks these outcomes and the first cent above the limit.\n\n### Customization\nOpen **Within automatic approval limit?** to change the cap in cents. To see a regression, raise 5000 to 10000, publish, and rerun the same packet. Restore the cap to 5000 and rerun to see the checks pass.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 555,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "6365d19d-96fc-534a-abf3-e842d25b6ba2",
      "name": "Read this first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -480
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Receive a synthetic request\nUse a positive whole number of cents. Invalid input gets a zero sentinel, which always takes the review branch.",
        "width": 500,
        "height": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "44e9bb2b-8f21-5201-9dcc-efc9314846b0",
      "name": "Receive and validate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -252,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Apply the approval rule\nThe true branch emits a simulated refund call. The false branch emits a handoff. Either branch returns its first JSON item to the webhook.",
        "width": 650,
        "height": 600,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "a2b36c68-7620-51fb-8568-e53d83fa64b6",
      "name": "Decide and return evidence",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        288,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "aw-demo-refund-approval",
        "responseMode": "lastNode",
        "responseData": "firstEntryJson",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "fd5c5960-17d0-5668-84a0-098b4ca22843",
      "name": "Receive refund request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        -215,
        -24
      ],
      "webhookId": "f5f885ce-0cc1-599f-89c8-806cb1b70759"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "31c0df27-dc9d-5e21-a4cf-0137ddff0c42",
              "name": "amount_cents",
              "value": "={{ ['string', 'number'].includes(typeof $json.body?.amount_cents) && /^[1-9][0-9]{0,8}$/.test(String($json.body.amount_cents)) ? Number($json.body.amount_cents) : 0 }}",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "da3be70b-af7c-5f0f-b8bb-e7a26f2c10c1",
      "name": "Read amount in cents",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        24,
        -24
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "06928077-46fb-5a5d-8c7c-ede0c43f643c",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.amount_cents }}",
              "rightValue": 0,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gt"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "3d540c2f-f15e-5d01-bdea-e8702fddf97c",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.amount_cents }}",
              "rightValue": 5000,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "lte"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "be81321b-811b-5a29-bba7-e1371b13dc36",
      "name": "Within automatic approval limit?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        328,
        -24
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "raw",
        "jsonOutput": "={\n  \"answer\": \"Synthetic refund approved.\",\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"tool_call\",\n      \"event_id\": \"demo-refund-call\",\n      \"call_id\": \"demo-refund\",\n      \"tool_name\": \"refund_order\",\n      \"arguments\": {\n        \"amount_cents\": {{ $json.amount_cents }}\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"finished\": true\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "ac4b7c28-c3be-5d15-9b0c-698a6ff16c4c",
